{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-22T18:29:20.995Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f93f297a00e60b66e8815dbe","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1549","lineage:pm-gh1549","lineage:pm-dj98","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-gh1549","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1549","lineage:pm-gh1549","lineage:pm-dj98","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.306","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-22T18:29:20.995Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-22T18:29:20.995Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Design: acquireLockLease returns {release, fence}. fence(commit) waits for the per-lock stale-cleanup gate (the same gate stale removal and lock publication hold), verifies the lease token under it, then runs the commit while still holding it, so a TTL/forced takeover cannot interleave with a fenced commit. mutateItem/deleteItem additionally compare the stored item bytes with the bytes read under the lock (stale_revision) to catch unlocked edits and extension-lock overrides, which have no file lease to verify. restore fences its write with the lease only (it already re-verifies item/history under the lock). acquireLock is now a thin wrapper over acquireLockLease, so every other caller keeps its exact contract. Heartbeat renewal deliberately NOT added: renewing created_at rewrites the lock file and races takeover; refusing at commit is the safe primitive, and callers can bound work with lease.expires_at from the refusal."}]}],"before_hash":"62a16f0e77bf7ba971bddcbe0b2fcf1a